WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.219 --> 00:00:03.052
(energetic music)

00:00:03.902 --> 00:00:06.506
- [Voiceover] When you're
looking out from the platform,

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:09.498
usually it's just water everywhere,

00:00:09.498 --> 00:00:11.965
which makes you feel really, really tiny

00:00:11.965 --> 00:00:14.465
jumping into this giant ocean.

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:23.257
I'm Rachelle Simpson, and I'm
a world champion cliff diver.

00:00:24.845 --> 00:00:27.453
It's very similar to Olympic diving.

00:00:27.453 --> 00:00:29.114
The only difference is that the end

00:00:29.114 --> 00:00:32.291
we're going to land on our feet.

00:00:32.291 --> 00:00:33.754
As I climb up on the platform,

00:00:33.754 --> 00:00:36.503
you hear the wind blowing in your ears.

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:40.165
Sometimes there's sea gulls
zooming around my head.

00:00:40.165 --> 00:00:42.714
To hear the announcer call my name

00:00:42.714 --> 00:00:45.263
it's kind of like I'm
falling into this hallway

00:00:45.263 --> 00:00:47.725
and the sound's slowing cutting out,

00:00:47.725 --> 00:00:51.885
because that's when I'm going into focus.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:55.903
That's when I set my feet
and then my arms go up.

00:00:55.903 --> 00:00:57.903
I count to three and go.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.295
Your body's on autopilot

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.954
and your brain is just
sitting back watching.

00:01:04.954 --> 00:01:06.812
Front somersault, full-twist,

00:01:06.812 --> 00:01:10.361
a second somersault, pike
position, a half-twist.

00:01:10.361 --> 00:01:13.055
(splashing)

00:01:13.055 --> 00:01:15.496
When you hit the water at
first you don't notice anything

00:01:15.496 --> 00:01:18.275
and then it starts all coming back.

00:01:18.275 --> 00:01:20.587
You create bubbles underneath the surface

00:01:20.587 --> 00:01:23.518
and you feel those bubbles
pushing you back up

00:01:23.518 --> 00:01:27.435
to the surface, quite a
cool feeling, actually.

00:01:28.659 --> 00:01:31.179
Then, you come up, take a breath of air,

00:01:31.179 --> 00:01:33.918
and the rush of adrenaline, it's
like you've been

00:01:33.918 --> 00:01:36.729
holding it off and not
even breathing until you

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:37.979
hit that water.

00:01:39.729 --> 00:01:43.849
Each time I enter the water
it's another successful moment

00:01:43.849 --> 00:01:47.259
of convincing my brain to
do something I'm scared of.

00:01:47.259 --> 00:01:51.272
Each time I get a sense of
empowerment when I overcome it.

00:01:51.272 --> 00:01:52.795
I love it.

00:01:52.795 --> 00:01:54.933
(splashing)

00:01:54.933 --> 00:01:57.933
(audience cheering)

00:01:59.053 --> 00:02:01.177
(successful music)

